From 1ce236b07adc966b62611583c0afaba1aad6fee6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Barbaros=20G=C3=B6ren?=
 <20913374+7tg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:13:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: the console's network as Wine's adapter, for
 GetAdaptersInfo

A title cannot start winedevice, so nsiproxy.sys never answers and every
NSI table fails: GetAdaptersInfo found no adapter. Blur's Demonware
client asks it before logging in and said the server was unavailable
without connecting (Amax, on the console; the same copy logs in on a PC).

The title reads the console's network with sceNetCtlGetInfo (Ethernet
address, IP address, netmask, default route; native/pw_net_ps5.c) and
passes it to Wine as WINE_PS5_ADAPTER=ip,netmask,gateway,mac
(src/pw_net_adapter.c checks each address, so only those characters reach
the environment). Wine patch 0480: when the NDIS table fails,
GetAdaptersInfo reports that one Ethernet adapter; without the variable,
as anywhere but in a title, nothing changes. iphlpapi joins PE_MODULES so
the patched DLL replaces the host build's. The log has a
"PW_WINE64 net adapter" line with each call's result.
